AB  - This work considers to numerically solve a multi-term time fractional diffusion equation with constant delay. First, we investigate the regularity of the solution and reveal that it possesses first-order differentiability in time, with the second-order derivative exhibiting singularity only at t=0. In view of the favorable smoothness of the solution, we develop a finite difference/finite element scheme for the considered problem using a uniform temporal mesh combined with L1 formulation and backward Euler formulation. To analyze the stability and convergence, a novel discrete sequence is introduced and its properties are discussed. By employing these properties, the unconditional stability of the numerical scheme is obtained and a new discrete fractional Gronwall inequality with delay is established. By using this Gronwall inequality, we obtain a local temporal error estimate for the proposed numerical scheme. Finally, some numerical tests are presented to validate the theoretical results.
