AB  - We consider the problem of recovering the space dependent source for a time-fractional diffusion equation with variable coefficients To obtain a reliable numerical solution, we propose a filter-based regularization method based on the singular system of a proper compact operator. An error estimate is derived under the assumption that the regularization parameter is determined by the Morozov discrepancy principle. As a result, as long as the unknown source satisfies a Hölder source condition, under smoothness assumptions that are often met in practical problems, we show that the error estimate can become close to O(δ), where δ denotes the level of noise in the data. For practical calculations, we propose a method based on a semi-discrete approach where spatial derivatives are properly discretized and the forward problem is stated as a time-varying ODE system. By doing so, we show that the regularization method proposed in the functional space setting is readily adapted to the discrete data case without any substantial modification. The method does not require any linear system solver and it is therefore easy to implement and inexpensive when compared to existing recovering source methods. Furthermore, an error bound for the discrete data case, with the same quality as that obtained in the functional space scenario, is derived. Numerical experiments involving 1D and 2D problems are provided to illustrate the effectiveness of the proposed method.
